# Abbie-First Product Rule

- Optimize for Abbie choosing to continue or replay, not adult-visible completion metrics.
- Put meaningful choice within 3 seconds and visible feedback after every action.
- Introduce a new reaction, decision, or surprise every 10–20 seconds.
- Avoid timers, penalties, lives, failure screens, and repeated actions unless they materially serve the game.
- Teach through the mechanic and story. Do not turn play into a quiz or lecture.
- Treat pedagogical interpretations as hypotheses to validate through observation, not diagnoses or labels.
- Rewards recognize participation, curiosity, helping, and completion—not artistic quality or compliance.
- Fictional currency unlocks permanent content only. Never add real-money purchases, ads, loot boxes, debt, expiring currency, streak loss, artificial scarcity, or fear of missing out.
- Parent controls must support unlock-all, refunds, balance correction, export, and reset.
- Descriptive creation dimensions such as NEW/SAME and WILD/NORMAL are neutral; neither side is better.
- A guide character may explain patterns but must never claim authority over whether Abbie’s art is good.
- Ship a small vertical slice to the real iPad and observe voluntary replay before expanding its art or levels.
